ks contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 38,520.24 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market pricing or budget constraints. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Review awardee A’s contracts for repeated purchases. Examine contract [1]’s details to see if it aligns with the body’s stated needs.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["JztfU638tJTN3k3tjedSGw%3D%3D","PjgoA%2Bn817pPpzdqOdhuWg%3D%3D","Opu%2Btb12cbzzAq95uGTrDQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}